  "result": "The gate returned **OK** (7 witnesses, 12 names, composes nothing) on its second run of the six-run budget. I used the first run by mistake before editing anything, so it judged the empty skeleton and returned `UNUSED_CLAIM`.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_307_12b.lean`):\n- **Class:** the subject is a member of `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`, written with `ru_aggregate`.\n- **Applicability:** some lane on a highway has a lane-control signal over it that shows `red_x` and faces the subject. \"Facing\" means the signal head lies ahead along the subject's heading, so the dot product of the vector from the subject to the head with its heading is above zero.\n- **Obligation:** for every lane and signal selected this way (the full selection is repeated inside the obligation), the subject must not:\n  - **enter** the lane: its occupancy of the lane must not start at that observation; and\n  - **drive in** the lane: it must not occupy the lane while `drv_motion_complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance)` fails.\n- **Narrowings:** none. The node already settles every reading, including the case of a vehicle at rest in the lane.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_307_12b.lean`): the scenes are on an eastbound two-lane highway with one signal over each lane, 80 m ahead of the start. They include the five scenarios the node planned, plus two I added so that each part of the formula changes a decided result:\n- `branch_2` (violated): the vehicle enters the red-X lane and is sampled at rest from that moment on. Only the \"enter\" condition catches it.\n- `branch_3` (not applicable): the vehicle is already 60 m past the red-X signal over its lane, so it is not facing it.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
